Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: attach imported dma-bufs to the 3D context

Objects created by importing a dma-buf of another device use
virtgpu_gem_dma_buf_funcs, which lacks the .open and .close callbacks that
regular virtio-gpu objects use to attach their resource to the 3D context of
the file and to detach it again.  The host is therefore never told that the
importing context may use the resource.  With DRM native context every later
reference to it is rejected ("invalid res_id") and the import fails, for
example when Mesa imports the udmabuf a Wayland compositor creates for a
wl_shm client buffer.

Use virtio_gpu_gem_object_open() and virtio_gpu_gem_object_close() for
imported objects too, so that they are attached to and detached from the 3D
context of every file holding a handle, like any other virtio-gpu object.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_prime.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_prime.c
index 70b3b836e..dc400c38c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_prime.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_prime.c
@@ -273,6 +273,8 @@ static int virtgpu_dma_buf_init_obj(struct drm_device *dev,
 }
 
 static const struct drm_gem_object_funcs virtgpu_gem_dma_buf_funcs = {
+	.open = virtio_gpu_gem_object_open,
+	.close = virtio_gpu_gem_object_close,
 	.free = virtgpu_dma_buf_free_obj,
 };
 
